% The Pit Takes One (resource scarcity: an irreversible fill)
%
% A ledge over a narrow pit. On the bridge across it squats a giant beetle;
% on the flooded walk beside it, a drone - a machine, already soaked. Both
% are bulky: the first body that falls into the pit fills it, and after
% that the pit takes nobody. Two companions, one skill each, from seven.
%
%   ledge (team) --- bridge (beetle) --- far
%     |                 |
%    walk (drone, flooded) --- pit (under the bridge and the walk)
%
% The beetle is an insect: the cold kills it (blizzard), and the pit takes
% it. Nothing else does. The drone is a wet machine: any jolt kills it
% (lightningFlash), and the pit takes it too. The pit is the scarce thing:
% it can take only one.
%
% Methods:
%   beetle in the pit   knock it off the bridge from the ledge (fireball),
%                       drag it across the pit from the far side (hook,
%                       taunt), or draw it down (vortex on the pit); then
%                       jolt the drone (lightningFlash)
%   freeze the beetle   ice the bridge (blizzard), and the pit is free for
%                       the drone - knocked or washed in from the ledge
%                       (fireball, tidalWave), drawn in (vortex) - or jolt
%                       the drone
%
% Traps:
%   - the drone is nearest the ledge and a push drops it: that fills the
%     pit, and with a mover and a jolt the beetle can no longer be taken;
%   - a wave from the ledge washes BOTH into the pit, and a vortex on the
%     pit draws both: whichever lands first fills it;
%   - blizzard on the flooded walk freezes the drone (a stun), not out.
%
% Hypothesis (design.md): no single skill wins; several pairs do, by
% methods of different kinds; with a mover and a jolt, the order is the
% puzzle.

% === Regions ===
region(ledge).
region(bridge).
region(far).
region(walk).
region(pit).
connected(ledge, bridge).
connected(bridge, ledge).
connected(bridge, far).
connected(far, bridge).
connected(ledge, walk).
connected(walk, ledge).
connected(bridge, pit).
connected(pit, bridge).
connected(walk, pit).
connected(pit, walk).
lineOfSight(ledge, bridge).
lineOfSight(ledge, walk).
lineOfSight(ledge, pit).
lineOfSight(far, bridge).
lineOfSight(far, pit).

% Push lines: from the ledge, off the bridge or off the walk, into the pit.
% From the far side, the pit lies between it and the bridge: a pull drops
% what it drags.
beyond(ledge, bridge, pit).
beyond(ledge, walk, pit).
beyond(far, pit, bridge).

onEnter(pit, chasm).
onEnter(walk, puddle).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, ledge).
at(mage, ledge).
mana(player, 2).
mana(mage, 2).

% === Enemies: both fill the pit when they fall ===
role(beetle, enemy).
at(beetle, bridge).
tag(beetle, insect).
tag(beetle, filler).

role(drone, enemy).
at(drone, walk).
tag(drone, machine).
tag(drone, filler).
tag(drone, wet).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, fireball).
knows(mage, lightningFlash).

% === Victory: both, in either order ===
win :- if(), do(neutralize(beetle), neutralize(drone)).
win :- if(), do(neutralize(drone), neutralize(beetle)).

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from seven (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(hook).
comboPool(taunt).
comboPool(vortex).
comboPool(blizzard).
comboPool(lightningFlash).
comboMinWins(10).
comboMinMethods(3).

goals(win).
